Subject: Wifi: local wireless MP client trace

ndsrecomp modification to vendored melonDS src/Wifi.cpp and src/Wifi.h
(GPLv3 5(a) notice; see patches/README.md for the convention).

Diagnostics only; no behaviour change. While the runner hook
nds_wifi_local_mp_trace_enabled() returns true (NDS_LOCAL_MP_TRACE=1 with
the local MP transport open), the MP client logs to stderr:

- each host frame it takes in CheckRX: cmd/ack/other, the frame's guest
  timestamp against USTimestamp ("ahead"), NextSync before and after,
  ComStatus and both reply TX slots;
- each SendMPReply: the reply slots, whether the previous reply is marked
  done, and the reply sent (address, length, duration, valid);
- a cmd dropped from RX as a duplicate (same sequence number);
- how many USTimer ticks it waited past NextSync for a host frame
  (MPClientMissStreak, a new member used only by the trace).

--- a/src/Wifi.h
+++ b/src/Wifi.h
@@ class Wifi, MP state
+    u32 MPClientMissStreak = 0; // latency trace only
--- a/src/Wifi.cpp
+++ b/src/Wifi.cpp
@@ (runner hook declarations)
+bool nds_wifi_local_mp_trace_enabled();
@@ Wifi::SendMPReply, before marking the previous reply done
+    trace: reply slots and previous reply state
@@ Wifi::SendMPReply, after the duration check
+    trace: reply sent
@@ Wifi::FinishRX, MP cmd sequence check
+    trace: duplicate cmd dropped
@@ Wifi::CheckRX, MP client sync
+    const u64 prevsync = NextSync;
+    trace: frame kind, timestamp vs USTimestamp, NextSync, slots
@@ Wifi::USTimer, MP client past NextSync
-            CheckRX(2);
+            const bool got = CheckRX(2);
+            trace: ticks waited for a host frame
